From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:38:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 022/111] Bring the running editor forward when another launch
 reaches it

libcosmic only unminimizes and activates the window when the launcher
passed an activation token, and it takes the token before the message
reaches the editor. A launch without one (a file manager that sends
none) left a minimized editor minimized and a background one behind.

The editor now unminimizes its main window and activates it with a token
of its own on every launch that reaches it. cosmic-comp gives an
unsandboxed client a focusing token; a sandboxed one gets the attention
flag. Activating a window that a launcher's token already focused
changes nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

